    "summary": "A shoulder cloth, a man&#039;s (?), with identical patterning at each end.  Ground made of apricot-coloured cloth predominantly; tabby woven (paired warps and wefts) using commercially made yarns.  White dotted patterning in centre field (white wefts).  Patterning comprises geometric motifs of different depths; a line of censers (?) divided by a bar, is the deepest band.  Worked in supplementary weft, &#039;khit&#039;, using white and black cotton yarns.  Warp ends raw.  Unworn.",
